  "notes": "TRANSITIVITY: Intransitive ({自動詞|じどうし}). Takes に particle: ～に{抗|あらが}う.\n\nCONJUGATION: Godan verb (wa-row): {抗|あらが}わない, {抗|あらが}います, {抗|あらが}って.\n\nNUANCE: {抗|あらが}う implies fighting against something powerful or seemingly inevitable (fate, authority, natural forces). It has a literary or dramatic quality.\n\nCOMMON COLLOCATIONS:\n- {運命|うんめい}/{宿命|しゅくめい}に{抗|あらが}う (to defy fate/destiny)\n- {権力|けんりょく}/{体制|たいせい}に{抗|あらが}う (to resist authority/the system)\n- {老化|ろうか}/{時間|じかん}に{抗|あらが}う (to fight aging/time)\n- {抗|あらが}えない (cannot resist/irresistible)\n\nRELATED WORDS:\n- {逆|さか}らう (to go against, oppose - more common)\n- {抵抗|ていこう}する (to resist - more formal)\n- {反抗|はんこう}する (to rebel - implies rebellion)",
